\medskip
\noindent{\small A fortress whose depth runs away until the win disappears; a
queen mating two kings by herself, on two rays at once; what ``both at once''
costs, a position this rule declines to call mate; a queen on the board,
nothing hanging, and White lost because two kings that guard each other have
sealed his king in the corner; and five kings on nine squares, whoever moves
first winning.}

